export const DISTILLED_GUIDELINES = "# Auckland Council Brand Guidelines — distilled reference\n\nSource: *AC Brand Guidelines June 2025* (64pp, `attached_assets/AC_Brand_Guidelines_June_2025_*.pdf`),\n*26-PRO-0516 Brand Guidelines contractors 2026*, and the live Frontify portal\n(https://aucklandcouncil.frontify.com/d/67jM5b5GuoL9). The operational subset lives in\n`brands.guidelines` (DB) and feeds every generation prompt; this file is the full reference.\n\n## Brand idea\n\n- **One purpose, one brand**: create an Auckland we can all be proud of. Every touchpoint uses the\n  pōhutukawa and kotahitanga patterns so work is attributed back to the council.\n- **Altogether Auckland** is the brand expression; kotahitanga (togetherness) is the core theme.\n- Strapline: **\"Tāmaki Turuki. Altogether Auckland.\"** — always lead with the te reo line.\n- Pōhutukawa symbolism: blossom = people coming together (kotahitanga), leaves = guardianship of\n  the environment (kaitiakitanga), waves = the waters that flank Tāmaki Makaurau. Chosen in 2010\n  when the eight councils amalgamated.\n\n## Voice & tone\n\n- Inclusive: dial up personal pronouns — you, your, our, we, us.\n- Talk like an Aucklander, not a bureaucrat: *let us know* (not \"notify us\"), *have your say*\n  (not \"consult with us\"), *aim/goal* (not \"objective\").\n- Headlines: no trailing full stop. Full stops on body copy only when there is other punctuation.\n- Supporting copy under a headline: max three lines.\n- Business-unit attribution goes in body copy where required: \"Auckland Council Pools and\n  Leisure.\", \"Auckland Council Holiday Parks.\", \"Auckland Council Holiday Places.\",\n  \"Auckland Council Libraries.\"\n\n## Pōhutukawa tile, grid, logos\n\n- **Master logo** = colour pōhutukawa in a **white square tile**. The mark is vertically aligned to\n  1/8 of the box (1/8 margin top and bottom), horizontally centred.\n- The tile is the **building block of the grid**: divide the artwork's shortest axis by an even\n  number of tiles — 4, 6 or 8 for print (\"A\" sizes usually 6), **1, 2 or 4 for digital**. One\n  division = tile size. Page margin = **1/3 tile height**.\n- Placement: primarily **bottom-right** of campaign artwork.\n- Colour logo on white or ≤20% colour/image density backgrounds; single-colour (white) version on\n  secondary colours, limited circumstances only.\n- **Corporate logos** (traditional lockups with wordmark) are reserved for: third-party funding\n  acknowledgement, building control, food safety, council/waste vehicles, all signage, uniforms,\n  contractor branding, documents/stationery.\n- Events: \"Auckland Council Events\" logo when council is majority funder; \"Proudly supported by\n  Auckland Council Events\" when partially funded. Clear space unit u = pōhutukawa height / 5;\n  minimum logo height 10mm / 50px. Full-colour versions on white/light backgrounds only.\n- Auckland \"A\" destination logo: only when >50% of audience is outside Auckland; teal #00a6a7.\n\n## The anther (framing device)\n\n- A large circle on a straight stem: circle centred horizontally with clear space for headline\n  copy above; stem enters from **left, lower-left 45°, or bottom centre — never 45° from the\n  lower-right**, and never covered by the pōhutukawa tile.\n- Size: extend to the margins, as big as reasonably possible, always showing straight stem lines.\n  Cropped anthers are subject to design review.\n- Stroke options: solid (same thickness as the logo's wave), gradient (double thickness), or none.\n- As a housing device: either copy inside the anther (image outside) or image inside (copy\n  outside). Backgrounds behind copy get a colour/opacity/multiply effect and must pass\n  accessibility contrast. Full-bleed photography variants: blur outside the anther (image inside in\n  focus) or the anther as a simple intersecting outline.\n- Not used inside carousel frames (makes imagery too small).\n\n## Kotahitanga patterns\n\n- Built from pōhutukawa elements + three tohu: **Te Ao Tūroa** (the enduring world),\n  **Whanaungatanga** (strengthening relationships), **Taonga Tuku Iho** (treasures handed on).\n- Used as subtle background texture: three-row wallpaper 30/20/10% opacity (bottom→top), two-row\n  20/10%, single row 20–30%. **Never more than 30% opacity.** Behind mid-artwork images ≤30%.\n- Stamp treatment: 2–3 patterns snapped to the grid, usually next to the pōhutukawa tile.\n- Patterns may use any brand colour.\n\n## Typography\n\n- **National 2** family (Kris Sowersby, Klim Type Foundry).\n  - Headlines: **National 2 Condensed Bold, ALL CAPS**.\n  - Headline support / subheads / CTAs / URLs: **National 2 Bold**.\n  - Body copy: **National 2 Regular**.\n  - **Rocked** script accent: sparingly, events/invite/celebrate collateral only.\n- Strapline treatment: usually two lines (\"Tāmaki Turuki.\" / \"Altogether Auckland.\"), height = 1/3\n  of the tile, aligned to margins; can run single-line or right-aligned beside the tile. Leading =\n  point size +15%. Te reo always first.\n- **Search-bar CTA**: pill with \"Search\" in National 2 Regular (tracking −10) + phrase in National\n  2 Bold (tracking +10), e.g. \"Search dog registration\". Can also carry a short URL.\n- **Hotspots**: short ALL-CAPS message set in a kotahitanga circle (e.g. \"AK HAVE YOUR SAY\");\n  crafted National 2 Condensed Bold product/programme marks (PEST FREE AUCKLAND, LIVE LIGHTLY) are\n  type treatments, **not logos**.\n\n## Colour palette\n\n| Group | Names & hexes |\n|---|---|\n| Core | Ocean `#11263d`, Anther Red `#de0a2b`, Pōhutukawa Leaf `#5b9c33`, Shore `#0073bd`, Kōwhai `#ffe104`, White `#ffffff` |\n| Vibrant | Ultra Violet `#3d2683`, Blush Response `#de006e`, Lemon Lime `#afca0b`, Shore Light `#00a7e5`, Tangerine Dream `#ef7d00` |\n| Dark base | Slate Grey `#3c3c3b`, Mocha `#691837`, Hunua Shadow `#1c473e`, Denim `#183a68`, Dark Chocolate `#4e2926`, Ocean 240 `#273652` (newsprint substitute for Ocean) |\n| Muted | Grey Lynn `#8e9ba4`, Amaranth `#e1a7bf`, Seagrass `#c4d28b`, Sky `#95d3e4`, Mascarpone `#f9e7c4` |\n\nBase every layout on Ocean + white/neutral grey; accents connect comms back to the logo.\n\n## Illustration style\n\n- Simple **flat vector**, snaps to the grid; built from logo elements — circles/ellipses from the\n  anther, leaf shapes, water curves. Rounded corners; arms as single heavy strokes with round caps.\n- **Three-plane scenes**: background, mid-ground (subject), foreground; a repeated object must be\n  ≥30% bigger in the foreground.\n- Established cast: faceless diverse people; native birds (tūī, pīwakawaka, kererū, korimako,\n  tauhou, riroriro, pūkeko, takahē); animals incl. dogs, ducks, hens, cows, sheep, horses, pigs.\n\n## Photography & video\n\n- Documentary style, the real Auckland: togetherness through diversity, pride, community; prefer\n  more than one person in shot; rich/bright/vibrant colour; playgrounds, beaches, paths, community\n  centres; avoid CBD-centric imagery. Landscapes and drone/aerials welcome. Events: vibrant,\n  upbeat, optimistic.\n- Video: animated pōhutukawa end-frame with strapline; watermark top-left; name keys are .mogrt\n  Premiere templates; captions required; keep top-left free of hotspots and bottom-right clear\n  (YouTube subscribe).\n\n## Social media rules\n\n- The pōhutukawa is the profile picture on council channels, so **1080×1080 organic/paid social\n  tiles carry no logo**; Facebook cover 820×360: no logo, no patterns.\n- Strapline is **not required** on social statics — \"less is more\"; on video it appears in the\n  blurred outro end-frame (4:5 Meta video: whiteout mono pōhutukawa + strapline PNG on final frame).\n- Meta content: first sentence carries the key message; keep creative single-minded (split multiple\n  messages into versions); ALL-CAPS/exclamation marks in primary copy hurt quality scores;\n  carousels 3–4 frames max, no anther in frames; CTA buttons/URLs unnecessary (links are overlaid).\n- Reels = awareness/entertainment (15–30s in-feed); Stories = drive a specific action (≤10–15s or\n  add a tap prompt).\n\n## Standard formats seen in guidelines\n\nPrint/posters (A sizes), digital screens 1920×1080 & 1080×1920, digital ads 300×250, 300×600,\n160×600, 728×90, video end-frames, social 1080×1350, 1200×628, 1080×1080 (no logo), Pinterest\n1000×1500, Meta story 1440×2560 (safe zones), Facebook cover 820×360.\n\n## Contractors (2026)\n\n- Co-branded clothing on all council jobs; simplified AC logo (no Māori strapline / \"working\n  together with\" text). Equal prominence with contractor logo. Placement order: wearer's left\n  chest (min 28mm) → right chest → under contractor logo → top of left sleeve. Front of safety\n  wear only, on solid colour. Full colour on white/light, white on dark, black on low-contrast/\n  hi-vis. Direct embroidery.\n";
